// =============================================================================
// Chora KnowledgeGraph Service (gRPC)
// =============================================================================
//
// Source-of-truth: docs/architecture/adrs/adr-143-per-user-knowledge-graph-hexagonal-fog.md
//   + chora-contracts/openapi/learner-knowledge-graph.yaml
//   + chora-contracts/proto/events/consumption/knowledge_graph.proto
//   + memory project_chora_data_plane.md
//
// Inter-service gRPC contract for the per-user Knowledge Graph aggregate
// family in Content Consumption (chora_consumption database, Team 1 / Content).
// REST surface in chora-contracts/openapi/learner-knowledge-graph.yaml is the
// learner-facing equivalent; gRPC is for internal service-to-service sync
// calls (mTLS via Cloud Service Mesh per CLAUDE.md §4 protocol strategy).
//
// Aggregates owned:
//   - MapCluster   — disconnected per-user knowledge map (the entity that
//                    Join merges)
//   - Exploration  — seed-rooted journey within a cluster
//   - HexagonNode  — cached focal + 6 neighbors (hybrid persistence)
//   - TrailHop     — append-only path history
//
// JunctionOpportunity is transient (computed via index probe over
// kg_hexagon_nodes; not persisted; surfaced via Subscription push).
//
// Primary callers:
//   - chora-bff-gateway   — fronts learner REST + GraphQL
//   - chora-consumption   — internal cross-aggregate calls
//   - chora-realtime      — WebSocket subscription resolvers
//
// Idempotency: every mutation RPC requires idempotency_key. Identical keys
// returning the same result.
//
// Deployed in chora-content (Team 1 pool). mTLS via Cloud Service Mesh;
// SPIFFE identity in mesh; W3C trace context in gRPC metadata.
// =============================================================================

